WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.760
The release of “The Matrix Resurrections” is just&nbsp;
around the corner, and Neo is all set to return.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.720
But how? Keep watching for a look at The One’s&nbsp;
backstory for a refresher on where we left off.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.800
In the 21st century,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.120
the Earth is devastated by a war between&nbsp;
humanity and the artificial intelligence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.840
they once enslaved. The machines then begin&nbsp;
capturing and eventually growing human beings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.480
and use their bodies' energy as fuel. The war&nbsp;
ends with the machines conquering the planet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:31.040
and humanity becoming essentially livestock,&nbsp;
bred by the machines and living their entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:35.120
lives in individual tanks to harvest&nbsp;
their heat and electrical energy better.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.120
To keep the humans docile, a sentient&nbsp;
program called The Architect devises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.400
a simulated reality called the Matrix to keep&nbsp;
human minds busy and unaware of their captivity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.400
The human mind can detect the unreality&nbsp;
of the Matrix, so each prisoner is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:54.240
given a subconscious choice to accept or&nbsp;
reject their simulated reality. Nearly 99%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.800
of prisoners choose the illusion, which&nbsp;
helps to sustain it as a consensus reality.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:04.880
The remaining 1 or 2% of humans unknowingly reject&nbsp;
the simulation. Most without even knowing it, use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:09.920
their collective disbelief to create an unbalance&nbsp;
known as the Architect's equation. To counter the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.880
imbalance, the Architect allows it to accumulate&nbsp;
in isolation. Once this "remainder" from his grand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:20.080
equation becomes too great to contain, the Matrix&nbsp;
randomly selects one human being to embody it.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.200
This person is known as “the One.” An&nbsp;
extraordinary individual is born who can learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:30.320
to reshape the Matrix at will. This figure awakens&nbsp;
and frees a number of humans to the real world.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.680
Once the One meets the Architect and&nbsp;
is told the truth about their nature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.920
they are given a choice to either cooperate&nbsp;
in perpetuating this cycle of control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:43.200
or to allow the Matrix to collapse, killing&nbsp;
all of humanity. Given two terrible options,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.360
the One chooses to repair the Matrix&nbsp;
so that it can be rebooted safely.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:52.000
Each set of freed humans believes that they are&nbsp;
the first resistance, released by the original One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.400
and destined to discover their reincarnation.&nbsp;
In fact, they are playing out a story written&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:01.280
by their enemy, over and over again. All&nbsp;
five iterations of the One before Neo chose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:05.920
to surrender to those machines and restart the&nbsp;
cycle. The story of the "Matrix" trilogy begins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:10.480
with the emergence of The Sixth One, Neo,&nbsp;
who is the first to make a different choice.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:15.360
“As long as the Matrix exists, the&nbsp;
human race will never be free.”

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.480
Like most humans, Neo is born in a vat in one&nbsp;
of the machines' farms. His brain is jacked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:25.360
into the Matrix from birth, and he is raised as&nbsp;
Thomas Anderson. Another unremarkable citizen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:30.240
of Mega City. He becomes a professional computer&nbsp;
programmer and moonlights as a hacker under the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:35.120
alias "Neo." Neo can sense that there's something&nbsp;
wrong with the world he lives in and spends his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:39.920
nights searching the Internet for clues as to its&nbsp;
true nature. This search puts him on the trail of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:45.200
a wanted terrorist known as Morpheus, who, as&nbsp;
it turns out, has also been looking for him.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.360
Morpheus reaches out to Neo via&nbsp;
his most trusted disciple, Trinity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:55.040
herself a famous and formidable hacker. Trinity&nbsp;
offers to help Neo find answers to his questions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:59.120
but their meeting attracts the attention of&nbsp;
the authorities, who come to arrest him at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.840
his workplace the next day. Morpheus attempts&nbsp;
to guide him to safety, but Neo does not have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:08.640
the courage to manage his escape and is captured&nbsp;
by the shadowy group known only as the Agents.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:12.640
While in government custody, Neo is&nbsp;
interrogated by the sinister Agent Smith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:18.160
for information about Morpheus. When Neo refuses&nbsp;
to cooperate, Smith demonstrates a terrifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:23.520
influence over reality, literally sealing Neo's&nbsp;
mouth shut and implanting him with a strange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.280
squid-like tracking device. Neo wakes&nbsp;
up at home afterward and dismisses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.840
this entire encounter as a dream — until&nbsp;
Trinity and her crew show him otherwise.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:37.520
Hungrier than ever for answers, Neo agrees to meet&nbsp;
with Morpheus, who offers him a choice represented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:42.400
by two pills. If Neo takes the blue pill, he&nbsp;
will return to his ordinary life and never hear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:46.960
from Morpheus again. If he takes the red pill,&nbsp;
Morpheus will give him the answers he seeks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.360
but there can be no going back. Neo chooses&nbsp;
knowledge but is completely unprepared for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:56.000
the terrifying truth. Soon, he wakes up in&nbsp;
the real world, a place he's never known.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:56.800
“This isn’t real?”

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.800
“What is real? How do you define real?”

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.680
Neo joins the crew of the Nebuchadnezzar,&nbsp;
a hovercraft commanded by Morpheus in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:10.720
service of the underground human Resistance. In&nbsp;
addition to defending Zion, the last human city,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:14.240
Resistance fighters broadcast their&nbsp;
consciousness back into the Matrix&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:18.320
in order to liberate the humans who&nbsp;
are still trapped there, one by one.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:22.960
Re-entering the Matrix as a free mind grants them&nbsp;
the ability to bend or even break the physical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:27.840
rules of the simulation. The Nebuchadnezzar's&nbsp;
technology can even download complex skill sets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:32.080
directly into their brains, making them&nbsp;
expert warriors overnight. With practice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:36.880
this will allow Neo to return to the Matrix&nbsp;
as an impossibly cool action hero like Trinity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:40.480
and the rest of the crew, but Morpheus&nbsp;
has even bigger plans for him.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:44.560
It's unknown how Morpheus comes&nbsp;
to suspect Neo of being the One,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:48.240
but Morpheus is certain that Neo&nbsp;
is the prophesied reincarnation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:52.880
of humanity's savior. Morpheus brings Neo&nbsp;
back into the Matrix to meet the Oracle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:58.240
who privately confirms Neo's doubts about himself.&nbsp;
Neo doesn't believe he's the One, and therefore he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:03.600
isn't. Morpheus, however, refuses to hear this,&nbsp;
and when the crew comes under attack by Agents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:08.800
Morpheus allows himself to be captured, so that&nbsp;
Neo can escape. Neo is unwilling to accept this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:14.000
sacrifice, and he and Trinity embark on a mission&nbsp;
to rescue Morpheus from Agent Smith's clutches.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:18.320
Neo and Trinity shoot, kick, and blast their&nbsp;
way through armed security and successfully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:22.480
return Morpheus's consciousness to his&nbsp;
body in the real world. Neo, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:27.120
gets cut off from their escape route and is&nbsp;
forced to fight Agent Smith one on one. Smith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:31.440
like all Agents, is a program endowed with&nbsp;
strength, speed, and endurance beyond even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:35.760
what a fully-trained Resistance fighter can&nbsp;
achieve. Neo wins the hand-to-hand battle and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:40.880
nearly escapes back into the real world, but it's&nbsp;
not enough — Smith recovers and shoots Neo dead.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:44.160
Back in the real world aboard the Nebuchadnezzar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:49.040
Trinity stands over Neo's apparently dead body&nbsp;
and whispers a secret into his ear. The Oracle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:52.720
once told her that she would fall in love&nbsp;
with a man, and that man would be the One.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:57.200
Trinity confesses that she's fallen in&nbsp;
love with Neo; therefore, Neo is the One.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:58.480
“I love you.”

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:09.040
Through the power of this belief, Neo's vitals&nbsp;
stabilize, and his projected self inside the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:14.640
Matrix springs back to life, more powerful than&nbsp;
ever. Neo can now see the code behind the Matrix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:18.720
move at speeds that are unfathomable even&nbsp;
to Agents, and stop a hail of bullets with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:23.760
a thought. With his newfound understanding of&nbsp;
the Matrix, Neo dives into Agent Smith's body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:26.400
and seemingly destroys his&nbsp;
program from the inside.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.560
Six months after Neo's death&nbsp;
and resurrection as the One,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:35.520
a massive machine army approaches Zion. With&nbsp;
no hope of winning this physical confrontation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:39.360
the crew of the Nebuchadnezzar embarks on&nbsp;
a mission to help Neo reach the Source,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:43.680
which the Oracle tells them will help them to win&nbsp;
the Machine War. They are led to The Keymaker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:47.760
who creates a backdoor in the Matrix through&nbsp;
which Neo can access the Source. In order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:53.200
ensure this operation's success, Trinity is forced&nbsp;
into battle with an Agent and is mortally wounded.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:57.040
When Neo steps through the backdoor, meets&nbsp;
another program, the Architect. Here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:01.600
the Architect reveals the terrible truth that&nbsp;
the One is actually part of the machines' plan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:06.240
another system of control. The Architect offers&nbsp;
Neo the same choice that he's offered the five&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:10.800
previous subjects of the Prime Program. He can&nbsp;
return his code to the Source and restart the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:16.160
cycle for another century, or refuse and allow&nbsp;
the Matrix to degrade and wipe out humanity.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.440
Every previous incarnation of the&nbsp;
One has been driven by compassion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:23.920
a general feeling of love that led them to&nbsp;
choose the long-term survival of the species.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:27.600
Neo, however, is in love with an&nbsp;
individual and can't bear to lose her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:32.560
Rather than perpetuate the cycle of the One,&nbsp;
Neo hurries back to the Matrix and to Trinity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:37.600
reviving her moments after death just as she once&nbsp;
did for him. Neo's choice means that the Matrix&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:42.320
now has an expiration date, but it also means&nbsp;
the fight for humanity's freedom can continue.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:48.080
Meanwhile, an additional threat grows from within&nbsp;
the Matrix that poses a danger to both humanity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:53.920
and the machines — Smith. After being decompiled&nbsp;
by Neo, Smith is reconstituted in the Matrix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:58.640
which reflexively recodes him as a counterbalance&nbsp;
against the power of the One. Smith gains the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:02.960
ability to rewrite the digital avatars&nbsp;
of other programs or even human beings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:06.640
creating countless copies of himself&nbsp;
that share a single consciousness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:09.360
Smith spreads like a plague across the Matrix.

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:13.520
Smith gains such power in the Matrix that the&nbsp;
machines have no counter against his influence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:17.120
The Oracle predicts that Smith's rage&nbsp;
and thirst for power will eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:20.880
consume not only the Matrix but the&nbsp;
real world, even the Source itself.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:26.480
“Seems like everytime we meet,&nbsp;
I got nothing but bad news.”

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:31.520
After Neo resuscitates Trinity, the couple returns&nbsp;
to the real world, where they escape from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:36.800
Nebuchadnezzar moments before machine sentinels&nbsp;
destroy it. To everyone's surprise — even Neo's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:41.680
— Neo is able to incapacitate a sentinel with his&nbsp;
mind. He determines that he can use his newfound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:46.240
abilities to journey safely through machine&nbsp;
territory to the physical home of the Source.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:51.120
Trinity refuses to let Neo take this dangerous&nbsp;
journey alone and accompanies him for the voyage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:56.000
aboard the hovercraft Logos. However, the&nbsp;
Logos also has a third passenger, Smith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:59.040
who has stowed away via the&nbsp;
hijacked human body of Bane.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:02.880
He attacks Neo and permanently blinds&nbsp;
him with a bare electrical cable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:07.520
While his eyes have been burned out, Neo can&nbsp;
still see machine code, including Smith. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:12.640
allows him to kill Smith's new body and to serve&nbsp;
as Trinity's navigator for the rest of the flight.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:16.800
Sadly, Neo's abilities prove insufficient&nbsp;
to protect the Logos from the Machine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:21.360
City's defenses. The Logos crashes,&nbsp;
fatally wounding Trinity. This time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:24.000
there's nothing to do but&nbsp;
give their tearful goodbyes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:28.560
After a final kiss, Trinity dies, and Neo&nbsp;
is forced to complete their quest alone.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:33.520
Neo travels to the heart of the Machine&nbsp;
City and confronts Deus Ex Machina,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:37.600
the machine figurehead. Neo offers to&nbsp;
re-enter the Matrix and rid it of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:42.000
threat of Smith in exchange for an end to&nbsp;
the war. The machine invasion of Zion halts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:47.360
while Neo does battle with Smith, who has now&nbsp;
assimilated the entire population of Mega City.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:52.080
Smith now has the ability to see the future and is&nbsp;
certain that the fight will end with Neo's death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:56.800
The battle rages, and Smith appears to get the&nbsp;
upper hand. Neo recognizes that the solution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:01.680
is to allow Smith to assimilate his code.&nbsp;
Smith absorbs Neo, therefore allowing Deus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:06.400
Ex Machina to destroy him and reboot the&nbsp;
system. This appears to kill Neo as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:12.000
but Smith is seemingly erased, restoring Mega City&nbsp;
and all the programs rewritten during his rampage.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:16.400
The Matrix is reborn, apparently under new&nbsp;
terms that will permit humans to leave if they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:20.560
so choose. This, as it turns out, has been&nbsp;
the Oracle's intention since the beginning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:25.440
of this cycle. Like everyone else, she placed&nbsp;
her faith in Neo, and her faith was rewarded.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:30.160
As the trilogy closes, the Oracle says that&nbsp;
she suspects that she'll see Neo again someday.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:34.320
Neo is indeed set to return in "The Matrix&nbsp;
Resurrections," though the nature of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:38.080
appearance in the film remains to be&nbsp;
seen. So we’ll just have to wait and see.

